  "stac_version": "1.1.0",
  "description": "## Snow Water Equivalent (SWE)\n\nSnow Water Equivalent (SWE) is the amount of water held in the snowpack — the depth of liquid water that would result if all the snow melted, given here in millimetres. It is a critical metric for estimating water availability, since the Alpine snowpack acts as a natural reservoir that releases its water through the melt season. This layer is a demonstration subset of Waterjade's Level-2 snow products, covering the 2022–2023 winter season over Tyrol, modelled daily at 500 m resolution with the SnowMaps processing chain and the GEOtop physical model. It builds on the snow-modelling work first developed within the Digital Twin of the Alps (DTA).",
